---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Presentation from "../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

import ThreeLedCountdownCircuitDiagram from "../../../assets/courses/foce/img/three-led-countdown-circuit-diagram.svg";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Figure1 = `for i in range(3):
    print("Beep")`;
const Figure2 = `Beep
Beep
Beep`;
const Task1 = `from machine import Pin
import time

led1 = Pin(28, Pin.OUT)
led2 = Pin(29, Pin.OUT)
led3 = Pin(30, Pin.OUT)

led1.value(1)
time.sleep(1)
led2.value(1)
time.sleep(1)
led3.value(1)
time.sleep(1)
`;
const Task2 = `from machine import Pin
import time

led1 = Pin(28, Pin.OUT)
led2 = Pin(29, Pin.OUT)
led3 = Pin(30, Pin.OUT)

led1.value(1)
time.sleep(1)
led2.value(1)
time.sleep(1)
led3.value(1)
time.sleep(1)

for i in range(5):
    led1.value(0)
    led2.value(0)
    led3.value(0)
    time.sleep(0.2)
    led1.value(1)
    led2.value(1)
    led3.value(1)
    time.sleep(0.2)

led1.value(0)
led2.value(0)
led3.value(0)
`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/foce/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Activity 2.4: Rocket Launch Countdown</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Activity 2.4</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">Rocket Launch Countdown</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Concepts</h2>
              <p>Cumulative Sequencing</p>
              <p>for Loops for Repetition</p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Today's Project: Mission Control</h2>
              <p>
                Three LEDs. T-minus 3, T-minus 2, T-minus 1 &mdash; then
                liftoff.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Not a Stoplight</h2>
              <p>
                A stoplight cycles &mdash; one light on at a time, forever.
                A countdown <b class="text-sn-theme">builds up</b> &mdash;
                each light joins the ones before it, staying lit, all the
                way to a climax.
              </p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Same LEDs a stoplight could use. Completely different
                behavior.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Repeating, Not Traversing</h2>
              <p>
                Every <code>for</code> loop you've written so far processed
                something &mdash; a range of numbers, a list. Sometimes a{" "}
                <code>for</code> loop just repeats an action a fixed
                number of times, and the loop variable is never used.
              </p>
              <Code code={Figure1} frame="code" lang="python" showLineNumbers={false} />
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Repeating, Not Traversing</h2>
              <Code code={Figure2} frame="terminal" lang="txt" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment"><code>i</code> is never printed &mdash; only its count matters.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Today's Objectives</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>Wiring three LEDs, each to their own GPIO pin</li>
                <li>Building a cumulative sequence with <code>Pin()</code> objects</li>
                <li>Using a <code>for</code> loop purely to repeat an action</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Terms</h2>
              <div class="text-start">
                <dl>
                  <dt>Cumulative Sequence</dt>
                  <dd>A sequence where each new step joins the ones before it, instead of replacing them.</dd>
                </dl>
              </div>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <p>
            Create a new MicroPython script named <b class="text-sn-theme">2-4-launch-countdown.py</b>.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 1: The Countdown</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Wire three LEDs (with resistors) to GPIO 28, 29, and 30.</li>
            <li>Turn them on one at a time, in sequence &mdash; without turning any of the previous ones off.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            All three sit next to each other in the block of eight pins on the
            top header. Note that the board prints them right to left, so
            reading along that block you will find{" "}
            <code>30</code>, then <code>29</code>, then <code>28</code> &mdash;
            the diagram below is a schematic, not a picture of the board.
          </p>

          <Image src={ThreeLedCountdownCircuitDiagram} alt="Circuit diagram showing three LEDs, each with its own resistor, wired to GPIO 28, 29, and 30, sharing a common GND" width={560} class="my-3" />

          <!-- PHOTO: all three LEDs wired and lit in sequence -->
          <div
            class="border border-secondary rounded p-4 my-3 text-center text-secondary"
            style="border-style: dashed !important;"
          >
            [PHOTO PLACEHOLDER &mdash; Task 1: Three LEDs Wired, Countdown Lit]
          </div>

          <Code code={Task1} frame="code" lang="python" title="2-4-launch-countdown.py" mark="8-13" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 2: Liftoff</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Once all three LEDs are lit, blink all three together rapidly 5 times, then turn everything off.</li>
          </ul>

          <Code code={Task2} frame="code" lang="python" title="2-4-launch-countdown.py" mark="15-23" ins="15-25" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Challenge (Optional): Accelerating Liftoff</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Make each countdown pause shorter than the last, so the countdown visibly speeds up toward liftoff.</li>
            <li>Wrap the entire sequence in <code>while True:</code> so it repeats continuously as a standing demo.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>When you run your script:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>All three LEDs should light up in sequence, each staying lit as the next one joins</li>
            <li>Once all three are lit, they should flash together rapidly several times</li>
            <li>Everything should turn off at the end</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer the following questions before submitting your work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>Why does this project's build-up behavior avoid feeling like a stoplight, even if you used the same colors a stoplight might use?</li>
            <li>In <code>for i in range(5):</code>, what is the loop actually controlling, since <code>i</code> itself is never used or printed?</li>
            <li>How does this circuit reuse the <code>Pin()</code> object pattern from Activity 2.3, just applied to three pins instead of one?</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Submit the required files to the appropriate dropbox.</p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Activity Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
